          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मनवाना — manvānā — \"to get (someone) to accept\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अरुण ने अपनी बात मीरा से मनवाई। Aruṇ ne apnī bāt Mīrā se manvāī. Arun got Mira to accept his point."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने अपनी बात मनवाई, usne apnī bāt manvāī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मनवाना (manvānā) is the causative of मानना, \"to accept\", which is inherited from Sanskrit manyate, \"thinks\" (CDIAL 9857): to make someone accept."
            }
          ]
        },
